    "text": "“Whatever countries charge the United States of America, we will charge them. No more, no less.” Anyone who travels outside the USA is well aware of how cheap most things in the USA are in comparison to other countries. And this isn't by a few dollars, but by significant factors. It was cheaper to buy a TV in the US, then to take it to the airline to ship to LatAm. $130 for the TV, $50 to ship, $50 to take it out of customs, and you'd still save $70.\nThis could save money for everyone in the world.",
